## Why This Is Asked
Tests mastery of CSS Grid for dynamic layouts, responsive behavior, and accessibility without JS. It also evaluates how candidates balance layout stability (masonry feel) with smooth entrances and motion controls.

## Key Concepts
- CSS Grid masonry technique with grid-auto-rows and grid-row-end: span
- Responsive grid breakpoints (3/2/1 columns)
- CSS-only toggle for mobile bottom sheet
- Entrance stagger and hover lift with prefers-reduced-motion
- Focus-visible accessibility

## Code Example
```javascript
/* CSS-like sketch (grid and card spans) */
.grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); grid-auto-rows: 8px; gap: 16px; }
.card { grid-row-end: span var(--span,18); border-radius: 8px; overflow: hidden; }
@media (max-width: 1024px) { .grid { grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr); } }
@media (max-width: 600px) { .grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } .rail { position: fixed; bottom: 0; width: 100%; } }
```

